* `install_progsf90()`, `install_renumf90()` and `install_genomic_programs()`
now raise `options(timeout)` to at least 600s for the duration of each
binary download (never lowering a higher user setting), so the UGA
server's slow connection no longer truncates the larger binaries under
R's 60s default. README.md, `?install_progsf90` and `DESCRIPTION` now
document the Linux MKL/OpenMP runtime requirement and the current UGA
certificate-chain workaround (#69)

* `install_progsf90()` now defaults its download directory to the same option
`check_progsf90()` uses. With no `bin/` directory yet (e.g. after installing
with `BREEDR_SKIP_INSTALL_BINARIES=true`), the old default resolved to an
empty path, and `install_progsf90()` -- the command the error message itself
recommends -- failed with "zero-length path argument" (#7)

* `build.AR.rho.grid()` now honours the `ar.eval` option instead of a
hard-coded grid, so a custom grid set with `breedR.setOption("ar.eval", ...)`
is actually used. `breedR.setOption()` also stopped collapsing a numeric
vector value (such as `ar.eval`) down to its first element (#6)

* `neighbours.at()`'s list method rejected every list of matrices: its guard
compared `class()` against `'matrix'`, which has included `'array'` since
R 4.0 and so was never `TRUE`. Unreachable from within the package, which
only ever calls the matrix method; affected only direct callers and the
competition integration test's setup (#27)

* `remlf90()` accepts `traits`, a named list selecting the responses on which
each random-effect group is fitted, so an effect can be dropped from some
traits of a multi-trait model. Unlisted groups keep every trait; absent
coefficients and variances are reported as `NA` (#51)

* `gibbsf90()` now returns the per-round variance component samples for any
model. `res$samples` held round numbers and component counts instead of the
variances unless the model had exactly one random effect and a single residual
variance; a multi-trait model returned nothing at all (#77)

* `remlf90()`, `remlf90_from_renum()` and `validate_prediction()` now refuse
class-based heterogeneous residual variances (`hetres_options(group_col = ...)`,
`OPTION hetres_int`). BLUPF90+ reads them under REML but fits a homoscedastic
model, which used to be returned without comment; `gibbsf90()` estimates
them (#39)

* `ranef()` now names the standard errors of genetic and generic effects like
their values, and labels the rows of multi-trait genetic effects by animal.
Looking either up by name used to return another level's (#60)

* Fix a crash in `parse_results()` ("replacement has length zero") on a fit
whose AI matrix needed bending on its last round; the `-2logL` line is now
searched for instead of assumed at a fixed offset from the last round (#24)

* Fix a crash in the AR `rho` grid search ("attempt to select less than one
element in get1index") when every candidate rho produced no usable
log-likelihood; it now reports a clear error instead (#3)

* `predf90()`'s `dir` argument is now required, with no default. Each fit now
works in its own subdirectory of `tempdir()`, so there is no longer a
directory that a default could point to (#25)

* Parse large covariance matrices more robustly from REML logs (#101)

* Store breedR model and REML log in temp dir for recovery (#100)

* More informative error messages on specification of initial variances (#79)

* Bugfixes (#80, #85, #86)

* Improved documentation (Handling pedigrees)


breedR 0.12
===========

* Basic multitrait interface  (#30)

* Default values for initial (co)variances are now a function of empirical
(co)variances

* Interface for using **weights** for residual variance  (#77)

* Vignette: Heterogeneous variances


breedR 0.11
===========

* Install breedR from package repository avoiding package devtools

* New vignette: Computing Heritability

* Access to inverse Average-Information matrix

* Automatic computation of heritability for genetic models and method 'ai'

* remlf90() interface to PROGSF90 OPTIONS

* Much more exhaustive testing ensures greater stability.

* New datasets Douglas (multi-site) and Larix (repeated measurements)

* Separate R-package from BLUPF90 binaries. Exploit 64bit architectures.

* Several bugfixes. Notably, the empirical variogram computation and memory issues with the AR model.



breedR 0.10
===========

* Full internal refactoring (with few 'visible' changes in the interface)

* `model.matrix()` no longer separates `fixed` and `random` effects.
  It returns the same structure as `ranef()` which is more intuitive.

* `vcov()` works now with any of the non-diagonal random effects.


breedR 0.9
==========

* New 'generic' model component allows passing a list of arbitrary incidence and covariance/precision matrices

* Optimized splines model. It runs about 5x faster.


breedR 0.8
==========

* New interface ranef() to access BLUP of random effects

* New interface model.matrix() to get incidence matrices

* Integrated vignettes into the package


breedR 0.7
==========

* Remote computing through ssh

* Convenient scaling of spatial variance components

* Additive genetic competition model

* Permanent environmental competition effect

* Simulation infrastructure


breedR 0.6
==========

* Visualization and diagnostic tools

* Prediction in unobserved locations


breedR 0.5
==========

* Customizable initial variance components

* breedR.option infrastructure


breedR 0.4
==========

* AR1xAR1 spatial model

* Eucalyptus Globulus dataset and demo


breedR 0.3
==========

* Pedigree checking, completing, sorting and recoding


breedR 0.2
==========

* Unstructured Random effects

* Simple simulation of spatially structured effects

* Spatial module following Cappa and Cantet (2007) splines model


breedR 0.1
==========

* Basic wrapper to Mistalz's (AI)REMLF90

* Convenient 'metagene' class to represent and manipulate simulated datasets
